# Page Layout

## Page shell convention

Every dashboard page under `src/app/(dashboard)/**` must use the `page-shell` utility class as its root wrapper. This class provides consistent responsive padding and max-width:

```css
/* defined in globals.css */
.page-shell  → mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 sm:py-10 lg:px-8
.page-header → mb-8 space-y-2 sm:mb-10
.page-title  → text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl
```

### Width variants

- **Default** — `page-shell` (max-w-7xl) for standard pages
- **Narrow** — `page-shell max-w-2xl` for forms (upload, edit profile)
- **Wide** — `page-shell max-w-6xl` for data tables (sales, admin)

### Rules

- Pages must NOT add their own `px-*` / `py-*` — `page-shell` handles responsive padding.
- Loading skeletons (`loading.tsx`) must also wrap in `page-shell`.
- Never use bare `space-y-*` as a root wrapper — it has no padding or max-width.
- Never use inline `px-4 py-8` instead of `page-shell`.

## Layout ownership

```
(dashboard)/layout.tsx  →  DashboardShell  →  SidebarNav + MobileDrawer
    └── profile/layout.tsx   → auth guard only, NO sidebar
    └── studio/layout.tsx    → auth guard only, NO sidebar
    └── admin/layout.tsx     → has its own sidebar (skips DashboardShell)
```

- `(dashboard)/layout.tsx` owns ALL dashboard navigation via `DashboardShell`.
- Child layouts (profile, studio) must ONLY contain auth guards or metadata — never sidebars or navigation.
- Child layouts must NEVER render `<aside>` or `<nav>` that duplicates parent navigation.

### Adding a new nav link

When adding a new dashboard page, add its nav link to **all three** files:

1. `src/components/layout/SidebarNav.tsx` — desktop sidebar
2. `src/components/layout/MobileDrawer.tsx` — mobile drawer
3. `src/components/layout/DashboardShell.tsx` — `allLinks` array for header title resolution

## Page structure template

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — server page with page-shell
export default async function SomePage() {
  const session = await auth();
  if (!session?.user) redirect("/login");

  const data = await someService.getData(session.user.id);

  return (
    <div className="page-shell">
      <div className="page-header">
        <h1 className="page-title">Page Title</h1>
        <p className="text-muted-foreground">Subtitle text</p>
      </div>
      <SomeClient data={data} />
    </div>
  );
}

// ✅ GOOD — loading skeleton with page-shell
export default function Loading() {
  return (
    <div className="page-shell">
      <Skeleton className="mb-8 h-8 w-44" />
      <Skeleton className="h-64 w-full rounded-xl" />
    </div>
  );
}

// ❌ BAD — bare space-y with no padding or max-width
export default async function SomePage() {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-6">
      <SomeClient data={data} />
    </div>
  );
}

// ❌ BAD — child layout with its own sidebar
export default async function ProfileLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <div className="flex">
      <aside><ProfileSubNav /></aside>
      <main>{children}</main>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## AppShell / DashboardShell separation

`AppShell` wraps ALL routes and provides:
- `<Navbar>` + `<Footer>` for public pages
- Bottom-player padding (`pb-36` / `pb-20`)
- Background gradient and `min-h`

`DashboardShell` wraps dashboard routes and provides:
- Sticky sidebar (`sticky top-0 h-screen`) + header
- Its own `min-h-screen` on the outer flex container

### Rules

- **AppShell must NOT apply `min-h`, `pb-*`, or background gradient to dashboard routes.** Dashboard pages have their own layout; extra height / padding from AppShell breaks `sticky` positioning on the sidebar.
- **DashboardShell's inner content column must NOT have `min-h-screen`** — only the outer flex container needs it. Redundant `min-h-screen` on nested elements inflates total height and causes the sidebar to scroll before sticking.
- **Never stack multiple `min-h-screen` declarations** on nested elements. Only the outermost dashboard container should set `min-h-screen`.
- When checking `isDashboardRoute` in AppShell, guard all layout-specific classes (min-height, padding, gradient) behind `!isDashboardRoute`.

### Sticky sidebar checklist

For `sticky top-0` to work correctly:
1. The sticky element must have a fixed height (`h-screen`).
2. Its scroll parent (body) must be the only scrolling context — no intermediate wrappers adding extra height.
3. No ancestor wrapper should apply padding or min-height that makes the page taller than the content.
4. The sidebar's inner content should use `overflow-y-auto` if nav items can exceed viewport height.
